\par
This Master Services Agreement ("Agreement") is entered into as of\par
_____________, 2010 (the "Effective Date") by and between Cairnwell\par
Technologies [CONFIRM EXACT REGISTERED NAME, ENTITY TYPE AND STATE OF\par
ORGANIZATION] ("Cairnwell"), and [CONFIRM ENTITY NAME -- Summit\par
Ticketing, LLC?] ("Client").\par
\par
This Agreement states the general terms that apply to any services\par
Cairnwell provides to Client. The specific services, fees, and related\par
details for a given engagement are set out in one or more Order Forms\par
signed by both parties and attached to this Agreement as exhibits. If\par
an Order Form conflicts with this Agreement, the Order Form controls\par
for that engagement only.\par
\par
\par
1. SERVICES\par
\par
Cairnwell will provide the services described in each Order Form.\par
Cairnwell is not obligated to provide any service not described in an\par
Order Form, and Client is not obligated to purchase any service beyond\par
what is described in an Order Form then in effect.\par
\par
\par
2. TERM\par
\par
This Agreement begins on the Effective Date and continues until all\par
Order Forms under it have ended. Each Order Form states its own term.\par
\par
\par
3. FEES; PAYMENT\par
\par
Client will pay the fees stated in the applicable Order Form. Amounts\par
not disputed in good faith within fifteen (15) days of invoice are due\par
net fifteen (15) days thereafter. Cairnwell may charge interest of\par
1.5% per month, or the maximum permitted by law if lower, on amounts\par
more than thirty (30) days past due. Costs Cairnwell pays to third\par
parties on Client's behalf (hardware, colocation, bandwidth, and\par
similar direct costs) are passed through at cost unless an Order Form\par
states otherwise.\par
\par
\par
4. RESPONSE; NO GUARANTEE OF REPAIR TIME\par
\par
During the hours stated in the applicable Order Form, Cairnwell will\par
acknowledge a report that a covered service is unavailable within one\par
(1) hour. Outside those hours, Cairnwell will provide a means of\par
contacting it and will respond when able, without a committed response\par
time. In no case does Cairnwell guarantee the time required to\par
diagnose or repair any problem. The parties acknowledge that this\par
section reflects the actual availability of a two-person company and\par
is not a service-level guarantee of any kind.\par
\par
\par
5. CLIENT RESPONSIBILITIES\par
\par
Client will provide Cairnwell with the access, credentials, and\par
information reasonably necessary to perform the services. Client will\par
use commercially reasonable efforts to ensure that any other person\par
with administrative access to a system covered by an Order Form\par
notifies Cairnwell before making a change to that system. If Cairnwell\par
must investigate a failure caused by a change of which it was not\par
notified, that time is billable at Cairnwell's then-current hourly\par
rate regardless of any monthly fee.\par
\par
\par
6. DIVISION OF RESPONSIBILITY\par
\par
Cairnwell is responsible for the infrastructure covered by an Order\par
Form: the operating system, and the specific applications, databases,\par
and services identified in that Order Form, to the extent of the\par
administrative and operational tasks described there. Cairnwell is not\par
responsible for the correctness of Client's application code or for\par
data errors caused by it. Where Client reports that a covered system\par
or service is not working and the cause has not yet been determined,\par
Cairnwell will investigate as part of the services covered by the\par
applicable Order Form; once the cause is identified, responsibility for\par
correction follows this section.\par
\par
\par
7. CONFIDENTIALITY\par
\par
Each party will protect the other's confidential information with the\par
same care it uses for its own confidential information, and will not\par
disclose it except to employees, contractors, and agents who need it to\par
perform this Agreement, or as required by law.\par
\par
\par
8. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY\par
\par
EXCEPT FOR A PARTY'S BREACH OF SECTION 7, NEITHER PARTY IS LIABLE TO\par
THE OTHER FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE\par
DAMAGES, OR FOR LOST PROFITS OR LOST DATA, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE\par
POSSIBILITY. CAIRNWELL'S TOTAL LIABILITY UNDER THIS AGREEMENT AND ALL\par
ORDER FORMS WILL NOT EXCEED $[__________].\par
